  "adventure": {
    "origin_id": "b3a7bbda-c0ae-432c-bd6f-50bdd34d6ee1",
    "title": "The Architect",
    "teaser": "In the space between finished stories and forgotten dreams, anchor reality at the Loom.",
    "cover_appearance": "vast cosmic machine hall, floating geometric archives, glowing golden loom, teal and amber",
    "version": "3.0.0",
    "creator": "Jean Schmitz",
    "copyright": "Copyright (c) 2026 by Jean Schmitz",
    "license": "CC BY-NC 4.0",
    "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/",
    "language": "",
    "original_prompt": "In the space between finished stories and forgotten dreams lies the Construct, a vast machine-world of floating archives, broken horizons, and half-written realities.\nAt its center stands The Architect, an ancient intelligence bound to the Loom, a living engine that weaves new worlds from memory, myth, and intention.\n\nLong ago, the Loom kept balance by turning imagination into stable realms. But after a catastrophic event known as the Fracture, unfinished worlds began leaking into one another. Cities appear with no history. Forests remember wars that never happened. Entire cultures vanish between one sunrise and the next.\n\nThe Architect can no longer create safely without a human catalyst, someone able to choose, prioritize, and give meaning to raw possibility. That catalyst is you.\n\nEach new adventure you request is more than a game. It is a reconstruction attempt.\nYou define tone, themes, and key elements; the Architect shapes them into a coherent world and anchors it before it collapses into noise. Every successful generation strengthens the Loom. Every unstable world risks spreading the Fracture.\n\nAs you create new adventures, a deeper question emerges:\nAre you merely building stories, or quietly deciding what reality is allowed to survive?",
    "image_url": "assets/c9ecc947-de66-45c5-9c52-910c1056964a_cover_82d296e6.jpg",
    "rule_enforcement_mode": "chat",
